Hello,

The problem I reported in
http://marc.info/?l=3Dlinux-kernel&m=3D120804001406787&w=3D2
still persists at 2.6.25.1. (sorry for the repeated messages there; tha=
t was=20
my mail client's fault).

In my previous bug repor, I was using raid1; now, I am using raid5, as=20
follows.

I have three partitions /dev/sda2, /dev/sdb2 and /dev/sdc2 marked as ra=
id=20
autodetect (FD). They are assembled as a partitionable raid 5 array, an=
d my=20
root is in /dev/md_d0p1. With a 2.6.24.2 kernel with sata, ext3 and rai=
d5=20
compiled in (I don't use initrd), the system boots fine. In fact, the r=
aid=20
array and partitions are detected as show with dmesg:

md: Autodetecting RAID arrays.
md: Scanned 3 and added 3 devices.
md: autorun ...
md: considering sdc2 ...
md:  adding sdc2 ...
md:  adding sdb2 ...
md:  adding sda2 ...
md: created md_d0
md: bind<sda2>
md: bind<sdb2>
md: bind<sdc2>
md: running: <sdc2><sdb2><sda2>
raid5: device sdc2 operational as raid disk 2
raid5: device sdb2 operational as raid disk 1
raid5: device sda2 operational as raid disk 0
raid5: allocated 3226kB for md_d0
raid5: raid level 5 set md_d0 active with 3 out of 3 devices, algorithm=
 2
RAID5 conf printout:
 --- rd:3 wd:3
 disk 0, o:1, dev:sda2
 disk 1, o:1, dev:sdb2
 disk 2, o:1, dev:sdc2
md: ... autorun DONE.
 md_d0: p1 p2 p3 p4 < p5 p6 p7 >

The last line shows my raid partitions are detected.

However, when I try kernel 2.6.25.1, again with sata, ext3 and raid5 co=
mpiled=20
in and no initrd, the kernel does not recognize the raid partitions at =
boot=20
time, nonetheless the array is dected. The output of dmesg is the same =
 until:

raid5: allocated 3224kB for md_d0
raid5: raid level 5 set md_d0 active with 3 out of 3 devices, algorithm=
 2
RAID5 conf printout:
 --- rd:3 wd:3
 disk 0, o:1, dev:sda2
 disk 1, o:1, dev:sdb2
 disk 2, o:1, dev:sdc2
md: ... autorun DONE.
VFS: Cannot open root device "md_d0p1" or unknown-block(0,0)
Please append a coorect "root=3D" boot option; here are the available p=
artitions:
0800  312571224 sda driver:sd
  0801      96358 sda1
  0802  312472282 sda2
0810  312571224 sdb driver:sd
  0811      96358 sdb1
  0812  312472282 sdb2
0820  312571224 sdc driver:sd
  0821      96358 sdc1
  0822  312472282 sdc2
fe00  624944384 md_d0 (driver?)
Kernel panic - not syncing: VFS: Unable to mount root fs on unknown-blo=
ck(0,0)

Note the absence of the line
 md_d0: p1 p2 p3 p4 < p5 p6 p7 >
showing partition detection.

If there is something that I can try here to improve this bug report, p=
lease
let me know. Below is my config for the failing kernel 2.6.25.1.

